##### 5. Eager Test (lines 53–65)

**Test:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds`

```csharp
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);
```

Seven distinct production methods called, but only one assertion on the final status. If this test fails, you cannot tell which step broke. No integration-test marker (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`) to justify this breadth.

**Fix — test one concern per method, or mark as integration:**

```csharp
[TestCategory("Integration")]
[TestMethod]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
```

Or split into focused tests: `ApplyDiscount_ReducesTotal`, `ReserveInventory_DecrementsStock`, etc.

**Risk if unfixed:** Expensive debugging — failures point at the wrong code.

